--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Meltemi (https://github.com/entro314-labs/meltemi)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are ported from the Meltemi project:

  sync cycle and folder handling      from `src-tauri/src/mail_sync.rs`
  JWZ threading                       from `src-tauri/src/threading.rs`
  HTML-to-visible-text extraction     from `src-tauri/src/model_text.rs`
  RFC 8601 Authentication-Results     from `src-tauri/src/auth_results.rs`
  bounce parsing and classification   from `src-tauri/src/dsn.rs`
  PGP/MIME shapes, detached-signature byte range, and the verdict ladder
  (`src/pgp.rs`)                      from `src-tauri/src/pgp_mail.rs`

`src/gmail.rs` takes its label-bits model, its history-expiry decision, and the
shape of its delta loop from `src-tauri/src/gmail.rs`.

`src/graph.rs` takes its delta-query state machine, its `@removed.reason`
distinction, and its Exchange datetime fallback ladder from
`src-tauri/src/graph.rs`.

Meltemi grants MPL-2.0 (Exhibit A only) on each of those donor files, naming
these derivatives, in its own LICENSING.md. Meltemi as a whole remains
all-rights-reserved; the grant is per-file, which is exactly MPL's boundary.

In every case the storage half is new rather than ported: the donor drove
SQLite, this drives a maildir.


